  "slides": [
    {
      "id": "slide-1-1",
      "sectionIndex": 0,
      "title": "What is Pre-training?",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "insight-box",
          "title": "The Foundation",
          "content": "<strong>Pre-training</strong> is teaching an LLM to predict the next {term:token:token} given previous tokens. It's like teaching a child to read by showing them billions of sentences."
        },
        {
          "type": "html",
          "content": "<strong>Objective:</strong> Learn general language patterns, facts, and reasoning abilities from massive text corpora.<br><br><strong>Scale:</strong> Trillions of {term:token:tokens}, thousands of GPUs, weeks to months of training."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "class": "uncertainty-table",
          "headers": [
            "Aspect",
            "Details"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "<strong>Data</strong>",
              "Web text (Common Crawl), books, Wikipedia, code (GitHub)"
            ],
            [
              "<strong>Objective</strong>",
              "Next token prediction (causal LM) or masked LM"
            ],
            [
              "<strong>Compute</strong>",
              "10²³ - 10²⁵ FLOPs for modern LLMs"
            ],
            [
              "<strong>Result</strong>",
              "Base model that can complete text but isn't instruction-following"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "slide-1-2",
      "sectionIndex": 0,
      "title": "The Pre-training Objective",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "id": "pretraining_loss",
          "label": "Cross-Entropy Loss (Next Token Prediction)",
          "parts": [
            {
              "type": "term",
              "key": "loss",
              "text": "L"
            },
            {
              "type": "operator",
              "symbol": "="
            },
            {
              "type": "raw",
              "text": "−"
            },
            {
              "type": "labeled-expression",
              "underline": "blue",
              "label": "Sum over all tokens",
              "labelColor": "summation",
              "popupKey": "summation",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "term",
                  "key": "summation",
                  "text": "Σ"
                },
                {
                  "type": "subscript",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "raw",
                      "text": "i"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "raw",
              "text": " log "
            },
            {
              "type": "labeled-expression",
              "underline": "orange",
              "label": "Model probability",
              "labelColor": "probability",
              "popupKey": "probability",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "term",
                  "key": "probability",
                  "text": "P"
                },
                {
                  "type": "subscript",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "term",
                      "key": "weights",
                      "text": "θ"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": "("
                },
                {
                  "type": "term",
                  "key": "token",
                  "text": "t"
                },
                {
                  "type": "subscript",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "raw",
                      "text": "i"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": " | "
                },
                {
                  "type": "term",
                  "key": "token",
                  "text": "t"
                },
                {
                  "type": "subscript",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "raw",
                      "text": "<i"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": ")"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "explanation": {
            "prefix": "<strong>In plain English:</strong> ",
            "template": "Minimize the negative log {term:probability:probability} of predicting the correct next {term:token:token} given all previous tokens. The {term:weights:model weights θ} are updated via {term:gradient:gradient descent}."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "insight-box",
          "title": "What happens during training?",
          "content": "1. Sample a batch of text sequences from {term:data:training data}<br>2. For each {term:token:token}, compute model's {term:probability:probability distribution} over vocabulary<br>3. Calculate {term:loss:cross-entropy loss} against ground truth<br>4. Backpropagate to compute {term:gradient:gradients}<br>5. Update {term:weights:weights} using optimizer (Adam, AdamW)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "slide-1-3",
      "sectionIndex": 0,
      "title": "Pre-training Results",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "insight-box",
          "title": "What the model learns",
          "content": "• <strong>Syntax & Grammar:</strong> Proper sentence structure<br>• <strong>World Knowledge:</strong> Facts about entities, events, concepts<br>• <strong>Reasoning Patterns:</strong> Logical chains, analogies<br>• <strong>Code Understanding:</strong> Programming languages, APIs<br>• <strong>Multilinguality:</strong> Many languages from diverse web data"
        },
        {
          "type": "insight-box",
          "title": "But there's a problem...",
          "content": "The base model predicts <em>likely continuations</em>, not <em>helpful responses</em>.<br><br><strong>Prompt:</strong> 'What is the capital of France?'<br><strong>Base Model:</strong> 'What is the capital of Germany? What is the capital of Italy?...' (continues the pattern)<br><br>We need <strong>fine-tuning</strong> to make it assistant-like!"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "class": "uncertainty-table",
          "headers": [
            "Model",
            "Training Tokens",
            "Parameters"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "GPT-3",
              "300B",
              "175B"
            ],
            [
              "LLaMA 2",
              "2T",
              "7B-70B"
            ],
            [
              "GPT-4",
              "~13T (estimated)",
              "~1.7T (estimated)"
            ],
            [
              "LLaMA 3",
              "15T+",
              "8B-405B"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "slide-2-1",
      "sectionIndex": 1,
      "title": "Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT)",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "insight-box",
          "title": "What is SFT?",
          "content": "<strong>SFT</strong> = Teaching the model to follow instructions by showing it (instruction, response) pairs.<br><br>Unlike pre-training which uses raw text, SFT uses <em>curated</em> high-quality examples of how an assistant should behave."
        },
        {
          "type": "html",
          "content": "<strong>Goal:</strong> Transform a text completion model into an instruction-following assistant."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "class": "uncertainty-table",
          "headers": [
            "Aspect",
            "Pre-training",
            "SFT"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "<strong>Data</strong>",
              "Raw internet text",
              "Curated (prompt, response) pairs"
            ],
            [
              "<strong>Scale</strong>",
              "Trillions of tokens",
              "Thousands to millions of examples"
            ],
            [
              "<strong>Objective</strong>",
              "Next token prediction",
              "Next token on response only"
            ],
            [
              "<strong>Quality</strong>",
              "Noisy, diverse",
              "High quality, consistent style"
            ],
            [
              "<strong>Result</strong>",
              "Text completion",
              "Instruction following"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "slide-2-2",
      "sectionIndex": 1,
      "title": "SFT Training Process",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "insight-box",
          "title": "Data Format",
          "content": "<strong>Input:</strong> '[INST] What is machine learning? [/INST]'<br><strong>Target:</strong> 'Machine learning is a subset of AI that enables systems to learn from data...'<br><br>The {term:loss:loss} is only computed on the <em>response</em> tokens, not the instruction."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "id": "sft_loss",
          "label": "SFT Loss (Response-Only)",
          "parts": [
            {
              "type": "term",
              "key": "loss",
              "text": "L"
            },
            {
              "type": "subscript",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": "SFT"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "operator",
              "symbol": "="
            },
            {
              "type": "raw",
              "text": "−"
            },
            {
              "type": "raw",
              "text": "Σ"
            },
            {
              "type": "subscript",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": "response"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "raw",
              "text": " log "
            },
            {
              "type": "term",
              "key": "probability",
              "text": "P"
            },
            {
              "type": "subscript",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "term",
                  "key": "weights",
                  "text": "θ"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "raw",
              "text": "("
            },
            {
              "type": "term",
              "key": "token",
              "text": "t"
            },
            {
              "type": "subscript",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": "i"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "raw",
              "text": " | instruction, "
            },
            {
              "type": "term",
              "key": "token",
              "text": "t"
            },
            {
              "type": "subscript",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": "<i"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "raw",
              "text": ")"
            }
          ],
          "explanation": {
            "prefix": "",
            "template": "Only the {term:token:tokens} in the response contribute to the {term:loss:loss}. The instruction provides context but isn't predicted."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "insight-box",
          "title": "Key Techniques",
          "content": "• <strong>LoRA/QLoRA:</strong> Parameter-efficient fine-tuning (freeze base, train adapters)<br>• <strong>Instruction Templates:</strong> Consistent format for prompts<br>• <strong>Chat Format:</strong> Multi-turn conversation structure<br>• <strong>Data Quality:</strong> More important than quantity"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "slide-2-3",
      "sectionIndex": 1,
      "title": "SFT Results & Limitations",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "insight-box",
          "title": "What SFT achieves",
          "content": "✅ Follows instructions<br>✅ Answers questions directly<br>✅ Maintains consistent persona<br>✅ Formats outputs properly (code, lists, etc.)"
        },
        {
          "type": "insight-box",
          "title": "But there are limitations...",
          "content": "❌ <strong>Imitates, doesn't optimize:</strong> Copies annotator behavior, good or bad<br>❌ <strong>Distribution mismatch:</strong> May struggle outside training distribution<br>❌ <strong>No preference learning:</strong> Doesn't know which of two good answers is <em>better</em><br><br>This is where <strong>RLHF</strong> comes in!"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "class": "uncertainty-table",
          "headers": [
            "Dataset",
            "Size",
            "Source"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Dolly",
              "15K",
              "Databricks employees"
            ],
            [
              "OpenAssistant",
              "161K",
              "Crowdsourced"
            ],
            [
              "Alpaca",
              "52K",
              "GPT-3.5 generated"
            ],
            [
              "UltraChat",
              "1.5M",
              "GPT-3.5/4 generated"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "slide-3-1",
      "sectionIndex": 2,
      "title": "Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "insight-box",
          "title": "What is RLHF?",
          "content": "<strong>RLHF</strong> = Using human preferences to train a {term:reward:reward model}, then optimizing the LLM to maximize that {term:reward:reward} while staying close to the SFT model.<br><br>It's teaching the model not just <em>what</em> to say, but <em>how well</em> to say it."
        },
        {
          "type": "html",
          "content": "<strong>The Three Steps:</strong><br>1. <strong>SFT</strong> - Create initial instruction-following model<br>2. <strong>Reward Model</strong> - Train model to predict human preferences<br>3. <strong>RL Optimization</strong> - Optimize {term:policy:policy} against {term:reward:reward} with {term:kl:KL} constraint"
        },
        {
          "type": "insight-box",
          "title": "Why not just use more SFT data?",
          "content": "• Human preferences are <em>comparative</em>: 'A is better than B' is easier to annotate than writing perfect responses<br>• SFT copies behavior; RLHF optimizes for <em>quality</em><br>• RLHF learns subtle preferences that are hard to explicitly write down"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "slide-3-2",
      "sectionIndex": 2,
      "title": "PPO: Proximal Policy Optimization",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "insight-box",
          "title": "The Classic RLHF Algorithm",
          "content": "<strong>PPO</strong> is the standard RL algorithm used in RLHF. It updates the {term:policy:policy} to maximize {term:reward:reward} while constraining how much the {term:policy:policy} can change in each step."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "id": "ppo_objective",
          "label": "PPO Objective",
          "parts": [
            {
              "type": "term",
              "key": "loss",
              "text": "L"
            },
            {
              "type": "subscript",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": "PPO"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "operator",
              "symbol": "="
            },
            {
              "type": "raw",
              "text": "𝔼["
            },
            {
              "type": "raw",
              "text": " min("
            },
            {
              "type": "labeled-expression",
              "underline": "blue",
              "label": "Ratio",
              "labelColor": "policy",
              "popupKey": "policy",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": "r("
                },
                {
                  "type": "term",
                  "key": "weights",
                  "text": "θ"
                },
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": ")"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "term",
              "key": "advantage",
              "text": "A"
            },
            {
              "type": "raw",
              "text": ", clip(r, 1−ε, 1+ε)"
            },
            {
              "type": "term",
              "key": "advantage",
              "text": "A"
            },
            {
              "type": "raw",
              "text": ") ]"
            },
            {
              "type": "raw",
              "text": " − β·"
            },
            {
              "type": "labeled-expression",
              "underline": "orange",
              "label": "KL Penalty",
              "labelColor": "kl",
              "popupKey": "kl",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "term",
                  "key": "kl",
                  "text": "KL"
                },
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": "("
                },
                {
                  "type": "term",
                  "key": "policy",
                  "text": "π"
                },
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": " || "
                },
                {
                  "type": "term",
                  "key": "reference",
                  "text": "π_ref"
                },
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": ")"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "explanation": {
            "prefix": "",
            "template": "Maximize {term:reward:reward} (via {term:advantage:advantage}) while keeping the {term:policy:policy} close to the {term:reference:reference model} using a {term:kl:KL divergence} penalty."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "insight-box",
          "title": "Key Components",
          "content": "• <strong>r(θ):</strong> Ratio of new to old {term:policy:policy} {term:probability:probabilities}<br>• <strong>{term:advantage:A}:</strong> How much better the action is than expected<br>• <strong>clip:</strong> Prevents too large updates<br>• <strong>{term:kl:KL} penalty:</strong> Prevents model from drifting too far from SFT"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "slide-3-3",
      "sectionIndex": 2,
      "title": "GRPO: Group Relative Policy Optimization",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "insight-box",
          "title": "A Simpler Alternative",
          "content": "<strong>GRPO</strong> (from DeepSeek) eliminates the need for a separate {term:value:value function} by computing {term:advantage:advantages} relative to a group of samples for the same prompt."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "id": "grpo_advantage",
          "label": "GRPO Advantage Estimation",
          "parts": [
            {
              "type": "term",
              "key": "advantage",
              "text": "A"
            },
            {
              "type": "subscript",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": "i"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "operator",
              "symbol": "="
            },
            {
              "type": "labeled-expression",
              "underline": "blue",
              "label": "Normalized reward",
              "labelColor": "reward",
              "popupKey": "reward",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": "("
                },
                {
                  "type": "term",
                  "key": "reward",
                  "text": "R"
                },
                {
                  "type": "subscript",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "raw",
                      "text": "i"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": " − mean("
                },
                {
                  "type": "term",
                  "key": "reward",
                  "text": "R"
                },
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": ")) / std("
                },
                {
                  "type": "term",
                  "key": "reward",
                  "text": "R"
                },
                {
                  "type": "raw",
                  "text": ")"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "explanation": {
            "prefix": "<strong>Key insight:</strong> ",
            "template": "Instead of learning a {term:value:value function}, GRPO samples multiple responses per prompt and uses the group's {term:reward:reward} statistics to compute relative {term:advantage:advantages}."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "class": "uncertainty-table",
          "headers": [
            "Aspect",
            "PPO",
            "GRPO"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "<strong>{term:value:Value} function</strong>",
              "Required (extra model)",
              "Not needed"
            ],
            [
              "<strong>Memory</strong>",
              "Higher (4 models)",
              "Lower (2-3 models)"
            ],
            [
              "<strong>Stability</strong>",
              "Sensitive to hyperparams",
              "More robust"
            ],
            [
              "<strong>Sample efficiency</strong>",
              "Better (learned baseline)",
              "Needs more samples per prompt"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "insight-box",
          "title": "Why GRPO is Popular",
          "content": "• Simpler implementation (no critic network)<br>• Used by DeepSeek for their R1 model<br>• Works well with verifiable rewards (math, code)<br>• Easier to scale"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}